//? Title: YOLO v2 priors, feature passthrough and WordTree fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify fit-only tensor IoU clustering, conditional hierarchy gradients, anchor/classification-only objectives and full20/9418-class graphs, then explicitly fit compact flat and joint detectors with multiscale inputs, paired BN checkpoints and actual scene galleries.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/yolo_v2.cpp`.

> The method

YOLO v2 adds dimension priors and fine-feature space-to-depth passthrough. YOLO9000-style WordTree supervision combines coarse detection boxes with fine image labels, selecting an objectness-weighted marginal prediction for classification-only examples.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/yolo_v2_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/yolo_v2_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/yolo_v2_concept.tikz > build/yolo_v2_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/yolo_v2_concept.svg build/yolo_v2_concept.dvi > build/yolo_v2_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
