> Conclusion

Flat detection selects epoch6 at validation AP50 .006284 and yields test AP50/AP75/AP50:95 .007700/0/.003289 with800 detections. Joint fitting selects epoch6 at validation AP50 .002315 and yields .002435/0/.000697 with800 detections. After only96 updates both detectors are still near their starting point: losses are falling, but held-out AP is close to zero and the galleries are dominated by spurious boxes. Much longer training is needed for useful detections; the small split, different objectives and update allocation do not establish an architecture ranking.

Tensor clustering, matching, hierarchy probabilities and both objective branches have independent fixtures before actual fitting. Full graph capacities and compact instructional fits are separate; restored held-out metrics and actual errors are retained without a benchmark claim.

> References

- [Redmon and Farhadi (2017), YOLO9000: Better, Faster, Stronger](https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.08242).
- [Authors’ Darknet implementation](https://github.com/pjreddie/darknet).
